36,-0.08677392452955246,-0.742447555065155,0.0,0.0,-0.01718909665942192,-0.5563884973526001,-0.001615410903468728,-1.7881377516459906e-06,0.0,0.0,-3.576278118089249e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.010692094452679157,-8.702239938429557e-06,-2.3841830625315197e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,4340,1657,8153,10747,374,894,6716,315,15279,11067,315,264,5792,12371,6113,448,3108,315,220,21,8153,30,17399,697,4226,304,44548,17855,1352,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nHow many units apart is any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with side of 6 units? Express your answer in simplest radical form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b0c864f27287856360fda3e11656a529cc49721449efde5d17ce3ded82e3d3d5"},"seconds":20.102813005447388,"seed":826206894747762082,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the distance between any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with a side length of \\(6\\) units, we can use the geometric properties of a regular hexagon. A regular hexagon can be divided into \\(6\\) equilateral triangles, each with a side length of \\(6\\) units.\n\n1. **Identify the structure**: Each side of the hexagon is \\(6\\) units, and the hexagon can be split into \\(6\\) equilateral triangles.\n\n2. **Determine the height of the equilateral triangle**: To find the distance between two parallel sides, we need to calculate the height of one of these equilateral triangles. The height \\(h\\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\(s\\) is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s\n   \\]\n   For our hexagon, \\(s = 6\\):\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Distance between parallel sides**: The distance between two parallel sides of the hexagon is twice the height of one of the equilateral triangles because the hexagon can be divided into two sets of equilateral triangles stacked on top of each other:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = 2 \\times 3\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the distance between any pair of parallel sides of the regular hexagon is \\(\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the distance between any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with a side length of \\(6\\) units, we can use the geometric properties of a regular hexagon. A regular hexagon can be divided into \\(6\\) equilateral triangles, each with a side length of \\(6\\) units.\n\n1. **Identify the structure**: Each side of the hexagon is \\(6\\) units, and the hexagon can be split into \\(6\\) equilateral triangles.\n\n2. **Determine the height of the equilateral triangle**: To find the distance between two parallel sides, we need to calculate the height of one of these equilateral triangles. The height \\(h\\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\(s\\) is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s\n   \\]\n   For our hexagon, \\(s = 6\\):\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Distance between parallel sides**: The distance between two parallel sides of the hexagon is twice the height of one of the equilateral triangles because the hexagon can be divided into two sets of equilateral triangles stacked on top of each other:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = 2 \\times 3\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the distance between any pair of parallel sides of the regular hexagon is \\(\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}\\).","id":"geometry:95"}
